- Release: https://github.com/AmrUser-48/agy-open/releases/tag/v0.7.2

2026-11-11 — FUNCTIONAL CHANGES

1. Multi-agent orchestration ("teamwork")

- Added /teamwork-preview to ask the planner for a validated plan without starting workers or modifying workspace files.
- Added /teamwork to execute plans as dependency-aware waves. Independent tasks can run concurrently; dependent tasks wait for successful prerequisites.
- Added configurable concurrency (maxWorkers, default 3, range 2–4) and support for staged plans of up to 12 tasks.
- Added custom-role delegation and per-role workspace scope, model, effort, concurrency, turn, tool-call, runtime, and output limits.
- Enforced permission inheritance: worker roles may narrow parent permissions but cannot widen a disabled or read-only parent boundary.
- Limited a plan to one writer. Writer work runs in an isolated snapshot; the coordinator validates patch whitespace/applicability and patch statistics, requests approval, and integrates the patch.
- Required a dependent read-only verification task after writer integration.
- Added bounded structured JSON artifacts for passing prerequisite findings to dependent workers.
- Added cancellation, per-role deadlines, partial-failure reporting, deterministic result collection, and bounded worker output.
- Added durable writer snapshots and /teamwork-recover for listing and validating recovery of interrupted work.
- Improved worker activity/history so redacted tool arguments, worker states, and recovery metadata remain visible and persisted.

2. Permissions, approval UI, and shell safety

- Restored expected workspace-write tool access for legacy built-in role files that omit allowedTools; explicit empty allowlists remain restrictive.
- Added/verified response-wide Allow in ASK mode using a/A; Allow once remains available separately.
- Corrected approval prompt terminal control-character rendering.
- Clarified and enforced role-level approval narrowing against the parent permission mode.
- Added an instruction-level safeguard against editing .profile, .bashrc, or system shell startup files merely to work around command-execution errors. Such edits require an explicit user request.

3. Session history and resume behavior

- Made session close reliable and idempotent, and propagated compression/file-close errors.
- Added/restored the CLI continuation path for the most recent saved conversation and explicit session restoration by ID.
- Added session-ID completion for /resume, /conversation, and /switch; explicit IDs also resume correctly in line mode.
- Set gzip as the final default for new session history files. gzip, zstd, and none remain supported.
- Preserved compatibility with historical .lzo-named files that actually contain Zstandard frames; legacy LZO settings normalize to Zstandard.
- Added tests for compression round-trips, legacy compatibility, and session restoration.

4. TUI commands and completion

- Added dynamic /agent role completion from configured roles; /agent opens the picker and /agent ROLE selects a role.
- Aligned slash-command completion metadata and added argument suggestions for supported command arguments, including effort, permissions, statusline, remote-control, title, plugins, theme, and sandbox.
- Cached recent session listings during completion to avoid repeated filesystem scans.
- Restored missing /ask, /approve, and /keybindings command routing/help coverage and corrected command descriptions.
- Removed the duplicate /agents TUI alias from registration, completion, dispatch, README, and REPL help. The standalone `agy agents` CLI subcommand is unchanged.
- Corrected line-mode Enter handling so slash commands are submitted and dispatched as typed; scoped the submit-on-enter behavior to the intended scrollback TUI mode.

5. OpenAI authentication and model access

- Added browser-based OpenAI/ChatGPT plan sign-in and model-entitlement checks.
- Fixed authorization URL construction and retry/consent handling for invalid_grant responses.
- Improved authentication diagnostics and added regression coverage.

6. Bash completion and installation

- Added a Bash completion installer and tests.
- Made completion helpers safe under errexit/nounset-style shell settings.
- Added completion for @-prefixed workspace paths, including top-level entries, and improved command/role completion coverage.

7. Documentation and regression coverage

- Expanded documentation for role permissions, custom role execution limits, teamwork preview/execution/recovery, session continuation, compression compatibility, and the lightweight Web UI.
- Added regression tests across orchestration planning/validation, concurrency, dependency scheduling, writer patch review/recovery, permissions, authentication, resume behavior, shell completion, and command completion.

